`nxf agent-manifest` emits nxf's declared contribution to the shared agent file (spec §6.2) as
data — the prime command and the SessionStart hook. Since nexus-flow-0lj.2 it carries no per-module
section: the `nxs` umbrella writes a single nxs-owned AGENTS.md discovery pointer instead. It needs
no workspace and is plugin-agnostic. The human form summarizes; `--json` is the machine contract.

```console
$ nxf agent-manifest

nexus-flow agent manifest
  prime command:  nxf prime
  hook:           SessionStart → nxf prime

Run with --json for the machine contract the `nxs` umbrella assembles from.


```

```console
$ nxf agent-manifest --json
{"prime_command":"nxf prime","hook":{"event":"SessionStart","command":"nxf prime"}}

```
